Permission allow rule (../../../.claude/settings.json): Write(.claude/**) is not matched by file permission checks — only Edit(path) rules are. Use Edit(.claude/**) instead (Edit rules cover all file-editing tools).
Two files had rules that applied: `a11y.md` and `form.md`.

The core bug is `CS-A11Y-001`: the invalid signal is keyed on `error` (one *cause* of invalidity) rather than the authoritative `validity`, and nothing is bound to the element that carries the role. A required-but-empty group (`valueMissing`) changes `validity` only — `changedProperties.has('error')` never runs, and even if it did, `role="radiogroup"` lives on the `<fieldset>` inside shadow DOM where a host-level attribute would never associate with it.

```js
/** Single authoritative predicate — not `error`, which is only one cause of invalidity. */
get isInvalid() {
  return this.validity !== undefined && this.validity !== 'valid';
}

updated(changedProperties) {
  // Mirror onto children on either signal, not just `error`.
  if (changedProperties.has('error') || changedProperties.has('validity')) {
    this.items.forEach((el) => {
      if (this.isInvalid) el.setAttribute('error', '');
      else el.removeAttribute('error');
    });
  }
}

render() {
  return html`
    <fieldset
      role="radiogroup"
      aria-required="${this.required ? 'true' : nothing}"
      aria-invalid="${this.isInvalid ? 'true' : nothing}"
      aria-describedby="${this.error ? 'error-message' : nothing}">
      <legend><slot name="legend"></slot></legend>
      <slot></slot>
      ${this.error
        ? html`<p id="error-message" role="alert">${this.error}</p>`
        : nothing}
    </fieldset>
  `;
}
```

What changed and why:

- **`get isInvalid()`** — one predicate, used by both `updated()` and `render()`. Per `CS-A11Y-002`, if you apply this to a sibling group component (checkbox-group), copy this *shape*, don't re-derive the predicate inline — that's exactly how the first pass of this fix shipped three different "is this invalid" expressions.
- **`aria-invalid` bound declaratively in `render()`, on the `<fieldset>`** — the element that carries `role="radiogroup"`. `radiogroup` is on ARIA 1.2's supported-role list for `aria-invalid`, so the attribute is valid here (`CS-A11Y-003`). Keeping `role="radiogroup"` is correct: it's a deliberate override of `<fieldset>`'s implicit `group` role, not redundant.
- **`aria-describedby`** links the message to the group, so the text is read as the group's description on focus — not only at the moment the live region fires.
- **Dropped `aria-live="assertive"`** — `role="alert"` already implies it; the pair is redundant and some AT double-announces it.
- **`nothing` instead of `"false"`** so the attributes are removed rather than set to a falsy-looking string.

One thing outside what you asked for, flagged rather than changed: `this.items` isn't shown here. If it's a live query of slotted children, note that `updated()` won't re-run when the slot's assigned nodes change — a radio added after the invalid state is set won't get the `error` attribute. A `slotchange` handler that re-applies from `isInvalid` covers it.
